<title>SPAIN: Spain June industrial production fell 5.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain June industrial production fell 5.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following provisional figures (percentage change):</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION		  JUN 96     MAY 96    JUN 95</p>
<p> Yr-yr					-5.7	  -3.2	6.6</p>
<p> Avg yr to date against yr ago	-2.7	  -2.0	7.9</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown (percentage change):</p>
<p>					     JUNE 96   MAY 96 YR-TO-DATE</p>
<p> Energy				     -2.9     -4.2    0.3</p>
<p> Non-energy minerals, chemicals     -5.6     -6.1   -4.3</p>
<p> Metals, precision tools		-3.7	0.1    0.3</p>
<p> Other manufacturing		    -8.9     -3.9   -5.8</p>
<p> Consumer goods			   -6.5     -2.0   -3.6</p>
<p> Capital goods			    -1.4     -0.9    1.1</p>
<p> Intermediary goods		     -6.4     -5.1   -3.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Year-to-date column gives average increases.</p>
</text>
